      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d6f17617",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who hold or are exposed to derogatory stereotypes about welfare recipients and overweight people, particularly those who may support or perpetuate ableist and classist narratives. The meme is designed to resonate with audiences familiar with 'welfare dependency tropes' and 'lazy/unemployed characterizations,' often found in conservative or economically-focused online communities that use visual humor to mock perceived laziness or public assistance dependence. The audience likely includes people who view obesity as a moral failing or a sign of personal failure, and who may be influenced by or reinforce 'burden on society claims' and 'ableism' in their discourse.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
